    {
      "id": "aaf16a4f-1e1e-4576-b909-0080a6f2fca7",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Vendor Invoice 3-Way Match & Payment Approval\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow captures a vendor invoice from a form, normalizes the submitted fields, and applies shared configuration such as the finance notification email. It checks Google Sheets for duplicate invoices, stops and notifies the submitter if one is found, or registers the invoice and retrieves the related purchase order and goods receipt. Custom code performs the 3-way match, then the workflow either marks the invoice ready for payment and notifies finance or places it on hold and sends an exception notification.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the invoice submission form fields so they provide the expected vendor, invoice, date, purchase order, and amount details used by the Set and matching nodes.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and point the duplicate check, invoice register, purchase order, goods receipt, and status update nodes to the correct spreadsheets/tabs and key columns.\n- Connect Gmail credentials for the duplicate, payment-ready, and exception notification nodes.\n- Set the financeEmail value in the Workflow Configuration node and verify the 3-Way Match Logic code matches your invoice, PO, and goods receipt column names.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the 3-way match code for accepted price or quantity tolerances, additional approval rules, or different exception reasons. Notification recipients and message templates can also be changed for AP, procurement, or vendor-facing workflows."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
